# Create Validator
## Validation Implementation
Place all validation under a new file in the same folder (../{feature-name}/components/filter/validators.tsx)
All validator error messages are examples, you should still look at the requirements of the feature to determine the correct error message

If the red * is required beside a form label, remember to add the required prop as such
```tsx
<Form.Item required></Form.Item>
```

### Simple Inline Validation
For validations with <= 2 conditions
```tsx
<Form.Item rule={[{required: true, message: 'Required'}, {min: 10, message: 'Minimum 10 char'}]}>{children}</Form.Item>
```

### Standard Integer Validator
For validations with > 2 conditions
```tsx
fieldNameValidator = (_, value) => {
  if (!isValidNumber(value)) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value < certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be less than ${certainValue}`);

  if (value > certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be more than ${certainValue}`)

  return Promise.resolve();
}
```

### Standard String Validator
```tsx
fieldNameValidator = (_, value) => {
  if (!value) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value.length < certainValue) return Promise.reject(`Minimum ${certainValue} characters`)

  if (value.length > certainValue) return Promise.reject(`Maximum ${certainValue} characters`)

  return Promise.resolve();
}
```

### Complex Validator
Sometimes validation will require values from other filter fields, in that case, pass in the getFieldValue() function to a curried validator
In rare cases, you may be required to pass in other functions to a validator

```tsx
fieldNameValidator = (value, getFieldValue) => {
  if (!isValidNumber(value)) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value < getFieldValue(EFilterField.otherField)) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be less than ${EFilterField.otherField}: ${getFieldValue(EFilterField.otherField)}`)

  if (value > getFieldValue(EFilterField.otherField)) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be more than ${EFilterField.otherField}: ${getFieldValue(EFilterField.otherField)}`)

  return Promise.resolve();

}
```

Another use case to create a curried validator is if there is  **total** logic overlap across the fields, where you can reduce code debt.
Assume the following code block all reference the same certainValue
```tsx
firstFieldNameValidator = (_, value) => {
  if (!isValidNumber(value)) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value < certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be less than ${certainValue}`);

  if (value > certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be more than ${certainValue}`)

  return Promise.resolve();
}

secondFieldNameValidator = (_, value) => {
  if (!isValidNumber(value)) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value < certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be less than ${certainValue}`);

  if (value > certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be more than ${certainValue}`)

  return Promise.resolve();
}

thirdFieldNameValidator = (_, value) => {
  if (!isValidNumber(value)) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value < certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be less than ${certainValue}`);

  if (value > certainValue) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be more than ${certainValue}`)

  return Promise.resolve();
}
```
We can simplify the logic into a singular factory to be used across all matching Form.Items
You may pass in certainValue here as a prop into the curried validator if it is not a store variable
**OR** getFieldValue/setFieldValue/validateFields... from Form.Item render functions
```tsx
checkCertainValueValidator = (value, certainValue?: any) => {
  if (!isValidNumber(value)) return Promise.reject('Required');

  if (value < getFieldValue(EFilterField.otherField)) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be less than ${certainValue}`)

  if (value > getFieldValue(EFilterField.otherField)) return Promise.reject(`${field} cannot be more than ${certainValue}`)

  return Promise.resolve();
}

<Form.Item name={EFieldName.first} rule={[validator: (_, value) => checkCertainValueValidator(value, certainValue)]}>

<Form.Item noStyle shouldUpdate>
  {({ getFieldValue }) => (
    <Form.Item 
      name={EFieldName.first} 
      rule={[validator: (_, value) => 
        checkCertainValueValidator(value, getFieldValue)]}
    >{children}
    </Form.Item>
    )
  }
</Form.Item>
```
